    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The player chose to activate Shadowspear's {1} ability (removing hexproof/indestructible from opponent's permanents) instead of casting a hand disruption spell or equipping Shadowspear. The opponent has no hexproof or indestructible permanents, so this ability accomplishes literally nothing - it wastes 1 mana for zero effect. The player's reasoning says 'equip Shadowspear to Nethergoyf' but they activated the wrong ability ({1} activated ability instead of the {2} equip ability). Meanwhile, they could have cast Thoughtseize or Inquisition of Kozilek to strip a card from the opponent's hand (the opponent likely has Kappa Cannoneer, Metallic Rebuke, or other threats), or they could have actually equipped Shadowspear to Nethergoyf for meaningful combat advantage with lifelink and trample.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Shadowspear's {1} ability to remove hexproof/indestructible from opponent's permanents, which had no effect since the opponent controls no such permanents.",
