    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Sonnet Coach has 3 untapped Swamps (one regular Swamp plus Urborg makes all lands Swamps, but only one Swamp appears untapped based on the board state). Looking more carefully: bf=[Swamp, Nethergoyf, {'name': 'Swamp', 'tapped': True}, {'name': 'Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth', 'tapped': True}, Shadowspear, Swamp]. There's one untapped Swamp and one other untapped Swamp, so 2 untapped black sources. They could cast Thoughtseize or Inquisition of Kozilek for 1 black mana to strip a card from the opponent's hand. The opponent has Emry on board which can recur artifacts, and seeing their hand is critical. They also skipped attacking with Nethergoyf (which has power equal to card types in graveyard - with Sorcery, Land, Enchantment in the graveyard that's 3/4). The opponent has Emry (1/2) as the only blocker. Attacking would deal at least 1 damage after blocks, or force a trade. Additionally, they could have played Ifnir Deadlands or Urborg from hand as a land drop. Passing the entire turn without casting a hand disruption spell, without playing a land, and without attacking is a significant waste of resources.",
