      "decision_index": 80,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The player's reasoning says they want to fetch Eldrazi Temple, but Prismatic Vista can only search for a basic land card. Eldrazi Temple is not a basic land. They will end up fetching a basic Swamp (which they already have 3 of on the battlefield). More importantly, the sequencing is suboptimal - they should cast Thoughtseize or Inquisition of Kozilek first before cracking Vista, since they want to see the opponent's hand to inform their decisions. Additionally, they have Thought-Knot Seer in hand which requires colorless mana ({3}{C}), and fetching a basic Swamp doesn't help cast it since Urborg makes all lands Swamps (producing black). They should have played Ifnir Deadlands from hand instead, which can tap for colorless mana naturally (or black via Urborg) and has utility as removal. Then they could cast a discard spell and still have Prismatic Vista available if needed later.",
